WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.580
There's no doubt that the follow-up to Avengers:
Infinity War will have a hugely dramatic effect

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.000
on the Marvel landscape.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.410
From the beginnings of a new era to the newcomers
who’ll lead the franchise into the future,

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.410
here are some of the many different ways that
Endgame could change the MCU… forever.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.610
The breaking of the fellowship

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:21.200
The precise details of actors' contracts can
be tricky to pin down, and it's only made

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.910
more difficult with MCU stars thanks to Marvel's
notoriously tight-lipped style of doing business.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.450
However, it’s clear that Endgame is the
end of the line for at least some, if not

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.090
nearly all, of the original six Avengers.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:38.551
Chris Hemsworth hinted in early 2018 that
he was hanging up his hammer as Thor, while

00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:42.550
Chris Evans teased an emotional farewell in
the fall of the same year.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.329
In addition, both Vanity Fair and Time have
reported that Endgame finds all six actors

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:50.120
either at or near the ends of their contracts.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.220
"I’m gonna miss these little talks of ours."

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.610
There's always the possibility of renegotiation:
Robert Downey Jr., for example, has already

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.140
extended his contract multiple times.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.980
But odds are that, one way or another, Endgame
is going to be the swan song for the saga’s

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.749
original band of heroes.

00:01:05.749 --> 00:01:09.789
It's a heartbreaking truth, of course, as
the MCU has largely revolved around these

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:11.750
characters for over a decade.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.470
But with so many new adventures on the horizon,
Marvel is sure to keep things exciting, even

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:20.679
if it's hard to imagine a Marvel Universe
where characters like Hulk, Thor, and Black

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:22.649
Widow aren't getting in on the action.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.649
Tony Stark

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:27.479
While there are many familiar faces that would
be missed after their departure from the MCU,

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:31.569
the hardest pill to swallow coming out of
Endgame will probably be the loss of Tony

00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:32.569
Stark.

00:01:32.569 --> 00:01:36.850
When Robert Downey Jr. told the press that
he wanted his MCU career to end on a high,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:41.359
the message was pretty clear: there weren’t
going to be any more contract extensions after

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:42.359
Endgame.

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:46.020
And sure, all good things do have to come
to an end, but the absence of Stark from the

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.399
larger storyline is almost impossible to imagine.

00:01:49.399 --> 00:01:54.570
The reformed billionaire playboy has managed
to influence nearly every corner of the MCU.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:58.959
He's been around since day one, was pivotal
in forming the Avengers, and has acted as

00:01:58.959 --> 00:02:02.439
a linchpin for the entire Infinity Saga storyline.

00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:06.869
Not only did he have that prophetic vision
in Age of Ultron, but Thanos' evident respect

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:11.600
for the hero just underscores how important
Tony Stark has been in terms of gluing the

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.780
MCU together.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.820
What happens when that glue is removed?

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.040
It's a question that will be answered soon
enough.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.040
Steve Rogers

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.050
Chris Evans alarmed fans when he penned what
appeared to be an emotional farewell after

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.210
he finished his last reshoots for Endgame
in October 2018.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:31.130
The uproar was quelled a little when Vanity
Fair reported co-director Joe Russo's comment

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:36.470
that Evans was "not done yet," but the Russo
brothers have toyed with fans' expectations

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.630
before, and no matter what either of them
might say publicly, all signs continue to

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:45.250
point to the likelihood that Steve Rogers
will finally hang up his shield in Avengers:

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.250
Endgame.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:50.090
Whether it comes via retirement or death,
the implications of Rogers’ departure from

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.340
the franchise are highly significant.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.690
Like Tony Stark, Steve Rogers has had a prolonged
impact on both the Avengers and the MCU as

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:58.690
a whole.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.440
He's served as the group's moral compass,
bringing a real sense of heart and soul to

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.890
the entire operation.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.700
New characters like Captain Marvel mean the
Avengers will have all the muscle they need

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.330
moving forward, but it's hard to imagine who
could take Captain America's place if he bows

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.510
out during Endgame.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:14.510
The death of a hero

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.460
Marvel has always had a hard time letting
go of their superheroes.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.520
No matter how tough the fight may be, the
sacrifices required have hardly ever resulted

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.320
in the literal, irrevocable death of a hero.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.490
During Captain America: Civil War, the worst
things to come out of the Avengers' devastating

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:33.290
feud were War Machine's injuries and a few
damaged relationships.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:38.390
The few seemingly-permanent superhero deaths
in the MCU have either been inflicted on one-off

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:42.850
characters or on those who still have at least
a pretty good chance of coming back.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:46.730
In Endgame, however, there's the distinct
possibility that we'll finally witness the

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.490
permanent death of a leading hero.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.990
"I got no plans tomorrow night."

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:55.050
Anthony and Joe Russo have remarked more than
once that they're determined to underscore

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:57.480
the action with real-world stakes.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:02.140
In an interview with Variety after Infinity
War’s release, the Russos warned fans that,

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:06.800
although remarkable things can happen in a
fantasy world, they have to come at an incredibly

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.970
high cost.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:12.410
If Endgame manages to finally let go of one
or more of the lead Avengers, say Captain

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:17.749
America or Iron Man, for example, it could
completely reshape the MCU canvas heading

00:04:17.749 --> 00:04:18.810
into Phase 4.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:19.810
Changing the tone

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:23.499
Endgame is primed to continue the shift in
tone that fans felt at the end of Infinity

00:04:23.499 --> 00:04:24.499
War.

00:04:24.499 --> 00:04:28.419
While there will always be films like Thor:
Ragnarok and the Guardians of the Galaxy franchise

00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:33.099
to keep audiences laughing, the future of
the MCU could be heading in a more serious

00:04:33.099 --> 00:04:34.099
direction.

00:04:34.099 --> 00:04:38.689
Up until recently, Marvel's universe has tended
to be bright and colorful, in its visual aesthetic

00:04:38.689 --> 00:04:40.490
as well as its dialogue.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:44.409
Comic relief was a constant presence, and
a certain self-awareness of the suspension

00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:46.479
of disbelief was always present.

00:04:46.479 --> 00:04:51.550
However, as Phase 3 wraps up, the future of
the MCU is looking more serious.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.650
Case in point: the Decimation.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:57.240
Infinity War ended with half of all life in
the universe gone.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:01.220
And while it was technically the first half
of a two-part story, the conclusion seems

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:06.310
to only be offering us another dose of heartbreak
as the team strives to fix the damage.

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:11.050
Is the end of Phase 3 simply a blip on the
otherwise lighthearted Marvel universe?

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:12.050
Not likely.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:16.699
The higher stakes in Endgame should have repercussions
that will be felt throughout the MCU for years

00:05:16.699 --> 00:05:17.699
to come.

00:05:17.699 --> 00:05:18.699
Coming together

00:05:18.699 --> 00:05:23.009
Up to now, the prime narrative of the MCU
so far has tended to focus on Earth-bound

00:05:23.009 --> 00:05:24.009
heroes.

00:05:24.009 --> 00:05:28.159
Sure, Thor came from Asgard, but even his
storylines usually moved between his own kingdom

00:05:28.159 --> 00:05:29.240
and Earth.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:33.499
Even some of the more mystical heroes such
as Doctor Strange have gotten drawn into the

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.199
Avengers’ action from time to time.

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:39.270
There's one group, though, that had never
met Earth’s mightiest heroes prior to Infinity

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.680
War: the Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:46.330
Throughout Infinity War, the two groups of
heroes crossed paths on Titan and in Wakanda.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:51.199
Despite some rocky beginnings, the two teams
eventually formed a united front against Thanos

00:05:51.199 --> 00:05:53.810
that was stronger than the Avengers could've
been alone.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.699
The trailers for Endgame have already shown
that the remaining Guardians and Avengers

00:05:57.699 --> 00:05:59.639
will continue to work together.

00:05:59.639 --> 00:06:03.839
That alliance is a fun one to watch play out
in Infinity War, and the possibility of seeing

00:06:03.839 --> 00:06:07.759
the two superhero groups working together
in the future is a tantalizing prospect.

00:06:07.759 --> 00:06:09.150
The New Avengers at the forefront

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:13.229
Marvel chief Kevin Feige has gone on record
to say that Captain Marvel wasn't just an

00:06:13.229 --> 00:06:18.059
exciting new face for the franchise, she was
also, quote, "as powerful a character as we've

00:06:18.059 --> 00:06:19.569
ever put in a movie."

00:06:19.569 --> 00:06:24.009
Feige’s confirmation that Carol Danvers
is the mightiest hero in the MCU hardly came

00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:28.939
as a surprise to anyone who saw Captain Marvel,
but the MCU’s head honcho also casually

00:06:28.939 --> 00:06:33.409
dropped a little more information on Danvers
regarding her future status in the franchise:

00:06:33.409 --> 00:06:37.889
"Captain Marvel is about to take the lead
and be the forefront of the entire cinematic

00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:39.389
universe."

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:44.289
While it's unclear just what "taking the lead"
will mean after Endgame's credits roll, Danvers

00:06:44.289 --> 00:06:47.779
is a great character to head up the MCU's
ongoing story.

00:06:47.779 --> 00:06:51.840
So will she actually lead the Avengers, as
some fans have taken Feige's statement to

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.840
mean?

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:56.870
The team already has a pair of de facto leaders
in Tony Stark and Steve Rogers… and with

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:01.460
Downey and Evans' contracts reportedly coming
to a close after this film, there's at least

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:05.360
a possibility that their interpretations could
turn out to be correct.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:09.369
Either way, it's at least nice to know that
Marvel has another leader already waiting

00:07:09.369 --> 00:07:14.409
in the wings, in addition to still under-explored
characters like Black Panther and Doctor Strange.

00:07:14.409 --> 00:07:18.979
Assuming they return to the MCU by the third
act of Endgame, there are plenty of leaders

00:07:18.979 --> 00:07:23.889
in addition to Danvers ready to take up the
Avengers' mission after Cap and Iron Man ride

00:07:23.889 --> 00:07:25.080
off into the sunset.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.080
Sagas

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.590
In an interview with Empire Magazine, Kevin
Feige dubbed the first 22 MCU movies "The

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:35.169
Infinity Saga," adding that Marvel executives,
quote, "wanted to bring to a conclusion a

00:07:35.169 --> 00:07:38.289
series of movies in a way that had never been
done before."

00:07:38.289 --> 00:07:42.469
It's a fitting name, as the stories of the
Infinity Stones have been interwoven throughout

00:07:42.469 --> 00:07:45.460
all three phases of the MCU so far.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:51.310
"One down, five to go."

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:56.199
While the Infinity Saga has been a heck of
a ride all on its own, one side effect of

00:07:56.199 --> 00:08:01.439
Feige's comment is that it has added yet another
layer to the categorization of MCU films.

00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:04.819
Now, in addition to "phases," we also have
"sagas."

00:08:04.819 --> 00:08:09.599
While anticipation for Phase 4 has long since
reached a fever pitch, especially with Marvel

00:08:09.599 --> 00:08:14.649
about to take nearly a year off before releasing
any new films, the next thing fans need Feige

00:08:14.649 --> 00:08:19.189
to reveal is what the next saga is going to
be titled… unless, of course, he's planning

00:08:19.189 --> 00:08:23.029
on waiting over ten years and 22 more movies
before doing so.

00:08:23.029 --> 00:08:24.029
The Quantum Realm

00:08:24.029 --> 00:08:27.740
The pair of Ant-Man films that took place
within the Infinity Saga didn't have too much

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.289
of an effect on the greater Avengers storyline.

00:08:30.289 --> 00:08:34.180
Sure, he showed up in supersize mode during
the airport encounter in Captain America:

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.640
Civil War, but that was about as far as his
role in the early MCU went.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:42.850
Even after Infinity War, Ant-Man and the Wasp
stayed fairly narrow in its scope until the

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:47.660
credits scene showed us the fate of the Pyms,
and where Scott Lang happened to be when Thanos

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.660
snapped.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:52.950
The second film, in particular, also dove
deep into the concept of the Quantum Realm.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:57.430
Hank Pym, Hope van Dyne, and Scott Lang spent
the majority of the story trying to get to

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:01.750
the Quantum Realm and back in order to try
to save Janet van Dyne, who returned with

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.310
a ton of new information about the mysterious,
otherworldly region.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:09.450
While Ant-Man and the Quantum Realm seem certain
to play a role in Endgame, Hank Pym actor

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:14.220
Michael Douglas took things a step further
during an interview on On Air with Ryan Seacrest.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.540
He explained:

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:21.040
"The Quantum Realm, that's the key.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.920
The Quantum Realm plays an important part
in all the next chapters, I think, of the

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:25.880
Marvel films."

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:26.880
Bigger costs

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:36.340
In early 2018 Disney revealed that, up to
that point, Avengers: Age of Ultron was the

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:42.170
most expensive Marvel film ever made, with
costs adding up to just shy of half a billion

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:43.170
dollars.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.170
Extravagant?

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.170
Perhaps.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:48.500
But with most of these blockbusters raking
in a billion or more at the box office alone,

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.620
the costs were more than justified.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.600
But the pricey productions didn't stop there.

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:57.130
The third and fourth Avengers films were rumored
to have a billion-dollar budget at their combined

00:09:57.130 --> 00:10:00.350
disposal, with both features being filmed
back to back.

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:05.140
That said, Disney's report also showed that
Infinity War reined in the expenses to just

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:10.290
under a third of a billion, leaving over $600
million available to finish off the story.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:14.480
While the astronomical size and scope of Endgame
certainly have the potential to easily use

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:19.460
up a budget that large, it begs the question:
how does that lavish spending change the standard

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:21.140
for future Marvel movies?

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:23.260
Is that going to be par for the course in
a few years?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:28.181
If so, you can bet your bottom dollar the
already impressive quality of most MCU films

00:10:28.181 --> 00:10:30.990
is about to be turned up a notch or two.

